<title>FRANCE: Pakistan may have bought Austrlian wheat -traders.</title>
<headline>Pakistan may have bought Austrlian wheat -traders.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grain traders said there was widespread talk on Thursday that Pakistan had bought 400,000 tonnes of Australian white wheat for June-July shipment.</p>
<p>The price of the reported deal was $171-172 per tonne, traders said, though there was no official confirmation.</p>
<p>One trader confirmed, however, that Australians had offered the lowest price to Pakistan's buyers and said that if the deal were finalised Australia would be the supplier.</p>
</text>
